/-!
# Literal threeCube table for the commutator power certificates

These binary candidates use bit j for column j, in the unchanged row convention.
Their names do not assert any matrix multiplication identity. The source script
proposes the rows; only subsequent Lean certificates establish the products.
The length, block widths and hint alignment are checked here. Hints themselves
are untrusted and the arithmetic checker validates each attempted shortcut.

Source: ATLAS M24G1-P1, positive words 3 and 4; see `../source/README.md`.
-/

